lcl@meceng.coe.northeastern.edu writes:
>
>With a level 12 priest made chaotic by wearing a helm of opposite
>alignment, I killed a peaceful white unicorn and, thinking to convert
>the alter from lawful to chaotic, tried to sacrifice it.  Oops.  Lost
>all my granted AC.  Following that, each sacrifice (as a chaotic on a
>chaotic altar) brings the message: "You have a feeling of inadequacy."
>I even sacrificed a Red Naga and still got the same message.  Does
>anyone know what gives?

If you're feeling adventurous, take off your helm of opposite alignment,
and sacrifice as a neutral on the chaotic altar.  You just might be
converted, (instead of the altar) and then it should only take a couple
of sacrifices to get in good standing.  Then, you can still use your
helm to be lawful whenever you want.

or, instead...

Heck, maybe you should start off fresh, keep trying your helm until you
become lawful, and then sacrifice at the chaotic altar.  Something will 
eventually convert (you or the altar) and then you should be in good 
standing with your newly aligned god....

Let us know what happens...

